WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:03.110
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:09.849
Today I’m going to explain an episode from
an American anthology “American Horror Story”

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:12.270
called “Monsters Among Us”.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.709
Spoilers ahead.

00:00:13.709 --> 00:00:18.539
Watch out and take care

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:24.060
The episode begins with a girl named Dot Tattler
telling us about the day, when the world as

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.769
she had known ended while walking into what
seems like a circus fair.

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:32.879
It was Saturday, the third of September, 1952.

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:38.070
She says the shadows that had sheltered her
were banished by the blinding lights of scrutiny.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.860
She knew she was entering the gates of hell
but like the inescapable pull of gravity,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.340
there was nothing she could do about it.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:50.899
The movie then cuts to a milk man arriving
at Eudora Tattler’s country farmhouse in

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:52.239
Jupiter, Florida.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:57.010
He notices that Mrs. Tattler still hasn’t
picked up her delivery from the other day.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:00.140
Worried, he ventures into her home to inspect.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:05.790
To his horror, he finds Mrs. Tattler’s brutally
murdered dead body lying next to the dining

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:06.790
table.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.620
He freaks out but decides to further investigate.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.170
He grabs a dough roller from the kitchen and
heads upstairs.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:18.510
He follows a strange noise coming from inside
a closet but only to freak out even more.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:22.570
The episode then cuts to an injured woman
being wheeled into an operating room.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:28.060
A nurse appears from the room with a look
of disgust in her face from what she witnesses

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.000
and vomits in the hall.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.110
The doctor examines the woman through an x-ray
machine and reveals that the injured woman

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:40.790
has one bladder, three kidneys, four lungs,
two hearts with a shared circulatory system.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:44.170
Later, a nurse reads a news article about
the incident.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:49.370
It says a wounded "monstrous creature", possibly
a blood relative of Mrs. Tattler, was found

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:50.370
in her home.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.220
who was thought to have lived alone.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:56.890
A candy stripper named Penny speculates that
the “monster” was Mrs. Tatler’s child

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.000
who she kept hidden from the world.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.220
A woman named Elsa Mars arrives and makes
small talk with Penny before asking her about

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:08.500
the “extraordinary creature” that’s
rumoured to have been brought in the hospital.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.750
Penny refuses to give her information about
the patient but Elsa appeals to Penny’s

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:17.750
young inner rebel and hands her a business
card that says Fraulein Elsa's Cabinet of

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:20.690
Curiosities, asking her to visit.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.120
Later, Elsa dresses up in Penny’s outfit
and makes her way into the Secure wing where

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.950
the patient has been kept.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:31.710
She peeks through the curtains to find a woman
with two heads sleeping on the bed.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:36.480
They are Dot and Bette Tattler, Mrs. Tattler’s
daughters.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.590
Elsa removes the curtains and wakes them up,
complimenting their beauty.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:44.540
She hands the sisters a balloon and reveals
that she dropped by their home to get them

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.540
a comfortable dress and because she is nosy.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:51.100
It turns out that the two sisters can communicate
telepathically.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:56.540
Dot has a serious demeanor and loves quiet
while Bette is more bubbly and likes watching

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.540
movies.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:02.330
Elsa fails to charm Dot, who sees through
her and is wary of her intentions but manages

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:05.870
to smooth talk Bette, comparing her to Jean
Arthur.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:10.350
She asks the girls about their sexlife and
boyfriends which makes Bette giggle while

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:12.650
Dot scoffs in disgust.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.780
Elsa then leaves the sisters alone but not
before promising to return.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.700
The scene then cuts to a couple, Troy Miller
and Bonnie Lipton making out by the lake Okeechobee.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:26.069
Suddenly, Troy runs to his car to fetch something.

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:30.510
As Bonnie waits for her lover to come back,
someone is seen coming out of the bush and

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.040
walking towards her.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:36.400
The girl finally notices the person and it
is revealed to be a clown.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.240
It has a creepy grinning mask on the lower
half of his face.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:45.310
Bonnie is scared of him at first but the clown
genuflects and gives her fake flowers, making

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:48.020
her feel more secure and comfortable.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:52.290
The clown then pulls out bowling pins from
his crown bag as Troy returns.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:56.280
Bonnie again gets nervous when she learns
that Troy didn’t hire him.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:01.510
The clown again pretends to genuflects and
knocks the couple out with the bowling pin.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:05.640
When Bonnie gains consciousness, she finds
the clown stabbing Troy to death with a pair

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.780
of scissors.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.510
Frightened, she attempts to run but the clown
catches up to her.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:15.800
At a diner, Elsa is cutting newspaper clippings
for her scrapbook about movies while other

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:19.830
patrons are reading about the horrific murder
at the Tattler house.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:24.040
Elsa notices a guy named Jimmy Darling, who
is wearing leather mittens, flirting with

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:28.990
a waitress on the other side of the diner,
which for some reason enrages her.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:33.490
She confronts him and calls him out for flirting
with girls while she worked her ass off to

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:36.400
find this new place that they can call home.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.430
Somewhere they can expand their show and build
an audience.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:44.340
Jimmy retorts that he overheard their landlord
asking her to leave and tells her she is living

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.580
in delusion.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:50.490
In a flashback sequence, Elsa is seen hanging
laundry while holding a two feet tall grown

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:55.800
woman named Ma Petite when her landlord Mr.
Haddonfield approaches and tells her that

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.020
he wants her to vacate his land.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:03.300
He wants to lease his land to someone else
who is willing to pay in advance and in cash.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:07.520
He tells her that even though she signed a
lease for a year, she hasn’t had any customers

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.000
for her show in two months.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.770
Moreover, Mr. Haddonfield’s wife doesn’t
like having the “freaks” staying in the

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:15.770
field.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:19.770
Elsa retorts that her monsters wouldn’t
hurt a fly and shows her landlord her silk

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.470
Belgian lingerie.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:25.490
She hands him her lingerie and invites her
into her room for “schnapps”.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:30.230
Back to the present, Elsa tells Jimmy to mind
his business when he wonders outloud how she

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:34.010
managed to convince the landlord to let them
stay for another month.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:39.090
She then tauntingly asks him what the waitress
he was flirting with would think of his “deformity”.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:43.930
Jimmy brushes her comment aside and tells
her that it is over, which only enrages Elsa

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:48.510
and she tells him that things are going to
change and she has a plan.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:52.681
The movie then cuts to a suburban home where
a group of housewives have gathered for a

00:05:52.681 --> 00:05:56.490
kitty party where they complain to each other
about their bad sex lives.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:06:02.540
A woman then appears from the back room, grinning,
strutting and smiling ear to ear as if someone

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.960
just laid some really good pipe on her.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:10.410
The host then approaches the shy wife among
the group and raves to her about a “roadside

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:11.410
attraction”.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:15.880
The shy wife then goes to the back bedroom
where Jimmy is waiting for her with his mittens

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:16.880
off.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.000
It turns out Jimmy’s hands are deformed.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:24.460
The woman lays on the bed and lifts her dress
up and Jimmy proceeds to do his magic.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.680
Back at the hospital, Elsa asks the girls
about the night their mother was murdered.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:31.080
Dot claims that it was a robbery gone bad.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:35.710
She says the robber got enraged when he realised
that they had nothing to steal and killed

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:38.550
their mother in anger before attacking them.

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:42.590
Bette adds that the man wore a fedora and
reeked of Aqua Velva.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:49.520
However, as Bette continues, Elsa recognizes
the plot from a hollywood movie called “Gaslight”.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.870
Elsa then reveals that she knows Mrs. Tattler
died two days ago before the sisters were

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.660
found with fresh wounds.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:59.460
She sees through their Bullshit and tells
them to get their story straight before the

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.030
police approaches them.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:04.550
Meanwhile, the creepy clown continues to go
on a crime spree.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:09.690
He brutally murders a couple, Jeffrey and
Mildred Bachman, in their home and abducts

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:11.830
their 8 year old son Corey.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:16.230
The series of murders and kidnappings in a
span of one month in an otherwise peaceful

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:21.950
town leads the police to believe that the
same maniac killed the Bachmans, Mrs Tattler,

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:25.000
Troy Miller and kidnapped Corey and Bonnie.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:29.920
The clown has held Corey and Bonnie captive
in a dilapidated trailer in what seems like

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.540
the middle of a jungle.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:36.250
Seeing the boy so frightened, the man tries
to get the boy to smile but only ends up scaring

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.860
him even more.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:41.479
Frustrated, the clown then starts throwing
things at the cage.

00:07:41.479 --> 00:07:46.080
Afraid of getting arrested, the Tattler sisters
run from the hospital but Elsa catches them

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.900
red handed at home preparing to flee.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.220
She accuses them of killing their mother.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:55.890
She speculates that Bette must have killed
Mrs. Tattler in a fit of rage when she won’t

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.610
take them to the movies or let them go out.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:03.840
Dot admits and claims Bette didn’t know
what she was doing, causing Elsa to speculate

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:08.310
that Dot stabbed Bette to make it seem like
they were also victimised by their mother’s

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:09.310
killer.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:13.169
Bette comes straight to the point and asks
what Elsa wants from them.

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:17.490
Elsa finally reveals her true intentions and
takes the sisters to her home.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:22.130
She plans to use them as the star attractions
of her freak show that features abnormally

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:23.169
developed people.

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.169
It is September 3.

00:08:25.169 --> 00:08:28.580
Bette journals in her diary about finally
being free.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:32.909
She is mesmerized by the silk, glamour and
lights of the circus.

00:08:32.909 --> 00:08:37.469
Meanwhile, Dot dreads the future and longs
for the quiet of the farm.

00:08:37.469 --> 00:08:43.779
Elsa’s freaks include Jimmy’s mother Ethel,
the bearded woman; Meep the geek; Pepper and

00:08:43.779 --> 00:08:44.779
others.

00:08:44.779 --> 00:08:48.639
Jimmy grows worried about the police looking
for the Tattler sisters but Elsa tells him

00:08:48.639 --> 00:08:50.699
that she plans to be their alibi.

00:08:50.699 --> 00:08:55.879
On Elsa’s orders Jimmy puts up a poster
of their show highlighting their star attractions:

00:08:55.879 --> 00:08:57.660
The Siamese sisters.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:03.339
A car full of young hooligans pass by and
harass Jimmy and other few freaks for being

00:09:03.339 --> 00:09:08.170
different, reminding Jimmy how the world treats
them differently because of their condition.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:12.800
Later that night, a disheveled Penny storms
into the dinning room and confronts Elsa for

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.069
drugging her.

00:09:14.069 --> 00:09:18.490
However, Elsa laughs her off and reminds her
that she willingly came with them.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:23.490
She shows Penny a footage of a happy Penny,
high as a kite, making out and performing

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:26.690
sexual acts with Jimmy and the others freaks.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:31.690
Stunned and horrified, Penny proceeds to leave,
threatening to tell the world about the depravity

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:36.139
of the freaks but Elsa stops her and tells
her that the real monsters are outside this

00:09:36.139 --> 00:09:37.809
tent in the suburbs.

00:09:37.809 --> 00:09:43.709
The bored, bitter, stifled, soul less housewives
who dream of strange erotic pleasures behind

00:09:43.709 --> 00:09:45.110
closed doors.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:49.880
Meanwhile, Elsa's monsters who others call
“depraved” are beautiful heroes who offer

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:54.889
their oddity, laugh, and fright to the people
in need of entertainment unabashedly.

00:09:54.889 --> 00:09:58.540
They lead the life they chose unlike others.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:03.120
The next day, Jimmy hands his mom the money
he made entertaining housewives and tells

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:06.470
her that he wants to leave the show to live
a normal life.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:10.610
But Ethel shuts him down and tells him this
is the “normal” for them.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:15.959
Later, Jimmy notices a detective inside Dot
and Bette’s tent proceeding to arrest them

00:10:15.959 --> 00:10:18.110
on suspicion of murdering their mother.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:22.110
Jimmy defends them, saying they wouldn’t
hurt a fly but the detective calls the twins

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:25.050
depraved monsters who could do anything.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:30.149
Fed up with being ridiculed and disrespected
for being different, Jimmy kills the detective

00:10:30.149 --> 00:10:31.509
in a fit of rage.

00:10:31.509 --> 00:10:36.709
For the first time Dot feels a sense of community
with the freaks and thanks Jimmy for saving

00:10:36.709 --> 00:10:37.709
them.

00:10:37.709 --> 00:10:43.449
That night, a snooty and entitled guy named
Dandy Mott and his mother Gloria sit in the

00:10:43.449 --> 00:10:45.800
audience waiting for the show to start.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:49.699
It is revealed Goria bought the entire show
just for her son.

00:10:49.699 --> 00:10:55.939
Soon, Ethel opens the show and introduces
the man with hands for arms, Pepper, Ma Petite

00:10:55.939 --> 00:10:57.899
and the Siamese sisters.

00:10:57.899 --> 00:11:02.850
Next, Elsa takes the stage and belts out a
David Bowie number with the freaks performing

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:03.850
behind her.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:08.810
Dandy develops a liking for Dot and Bette
and after the performance, Gloria tells Elsa

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:14.519
she wants to buy the twins for her son, revealing
she is willing to go as high as $15,000.

00:11:14.519 --> 00:11:19.970
However, Dot and Bette turn down the offer
saying the freaks show is their home.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:25.009
Upset, Gloria makes fun of Elsa calling her
attempt at singing “pathetic” and “the

00:11:25.009 --> 00:11:28.360
most freakish thing of all tonight” before
storming out.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:33.250
Afterwards, Jimmy leads a procession of the
freaks to bury the detective in the woods.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:37.830
He delivers a passionate speech, calling out
how badly the world treats them.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:42.439
He says if the world wants to call them monsters
without even knowing them, then they will

00:11:42.439 --> 00:11:44.259
act like monsters.

00:11:44.259 --> 00:11:48.699
He vows that if anyone tries to mess with
them from now on, they will end up like the

00:11:48.699 --> 00:11:49.730
detective.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:54.699
The freaks then converge near the detective
and hack him to bits as the clown watches

00:11:54.699 --> 00:11:56.910
it transpire from a distance.

00:11:56.910 --> 00:12:00.949
Later, when Elsa skips dinner, Ethel brings
food to her tent.

00:12:00.949 --> 00:12:04.819
It seems Gloria’s words seem to have taken
a toll on Elsa’s mind.

00:12:04.819 --> 00:12:09.029
When Ethel thanks Elsa for saving them by
bringing the twin sisters, Elsa confesses

00:12:09.029 --> 00:12:14.019
that she didn’t bring the twins to save
the show, she brought them to save herself.

00:12:14.019 --> 00:12:18.759
Elsa has always wanted to become a star but
now she wonders if it’s too late for her.

00:12:18.759 --> 00:12:23.689
Taking Elsa’s opium pipe away, Ethel assures
her that she is gifted and meant to become

00:12:23.689 --> 00:12:25.339
a household name.

00:12:25.339 --> 00:12:30.220
After Ethel leaves, Elsa puts on some music
and takes off her pantyhose, revealing her

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.949
artificial legs.

